{
  "id": "semiconductor-laser-turn-on-third-science",
  "name": "Semiconductor laser carrier-photon turn-on and relaxation",
  "description": "Stimulated emission couples population inversion to photon growth, with a source threshold and relaxation transient. Single-mode density model; omits optical phase, spatial hole burning, thermal changes and stochastic emission. No actual laser calibration. Illustrative normalized pump1500,carrier lifetime1,photon lifetime0.02,differential gain0.05,transparency10,beta0.0001;initial carriers0,photons1e-6,loss0;horizon10,Radau output0.01. Confinement1 and gain compression0; added cumulative lost-quanta budget is our accounting variable. Original mathematical transcription/adaptation; not a calibrated forecast. Signed net-rate flows implement the stated equations. No numerical clamps or hidden resets.",
  "category": "physics",
  "source": "https://courses.ece.ucsb.edu/ECE228/228B_S09Blumenthal/Lecture4_228B_S09_Final.pdf",
  "reference": "UCSB ECE228B2009, Laser Rate Equations; carrier/photon densities and stimulated/spontaneous terms. Also first-party https://docs.flexcompute.com/projects/photonforge/en/latest/guides/Directly_Modulated_Laser.html .",
